-<section class="card" style="margin-top:20px"><div class="eyebrow">Section 3</div><h2 class="section-title">Money-flow logic</h2><ol style="line-height:1.8;color:var(--muted)"><li><b>Deposit:</b> increases Account.total_balance, the selected Allocation.balance and the matching MoneyPool.current_amount.</li><li><b>Expense:</b> decreases those three values together and creates one ledger Transaction.</li><li><b>Wallet transfer:</b> creates an outgoing transaction on the source wallet and an incoming transaction on the destination wallet, linked through related_tx.</li><li><b>Reconciliation:</b> Account.total_balance must equal the sum of its allocations and the sum of its money pools; failed reconciliation aborts the transaction.</li><li><b>Expense taxonomy:</b> Category is the broad bucket, SubCategory refines it, Item identifies the fixed master item, while Transaction.variant remains deliberately free text for unpredictable details such as a brand, provider or food variant.</li><li><b>Food taxonomy:</b> FoodProfile extends a food Item with Food/Drink type, food group, health classification and sugary status. These attributes can be queried through the Item → FoodProfile relationship.</li></ol></section>
-{% endblock %}
